Cold-restore a dead agent pane on a headless host

After a workspace restart, opening an agent pane in the tile renders its full
transcript in chat view while typing in the composer lands in a shell:
`bash: command not found`.

Upstream already owns the whole resume - `ensureAgentSession` runs the
execution-owner check, signs the session claim, builds the resume startup plan
and spawns in the background path `createTerminal` added for a serve host with
no renderer window (#10333). What it cannot do headless is know WHICH session to
resume: that request normally comes from the renderer, and `orca serve` has
none, which is why it refuses `kind: 'automatic'` outright.

So this supplies only the request. `resolveHeadlessAgentColdRestore` reads the
agent and provider session off this host's agent-hook rows - disk-hydrated at
startup, so they survive the restart that killed the agent - and hands them to
`ensureAgentSession` as an explicit one. A configured `tab.launchAgent` outranks
the hook row and a disagreement drops the resume, since agent and provider
session must move together. A refused or unresolvable resume falls through to
the plain materialize rather than leaving the tab untappable.

To test, restart the workspace, open an agent pane in the tile and continue the
conversation: the agent should answer with full prior context and run shell
commands. Covered by `headless-agent-cold-restore.test.ts` and
`headless-agent-cold-restore-precedence.test.ts`.
